<%- include("partials/head") %>
<%- include("partials/header") %>
<main>
<%- include("partials/phero", {
  crumbs: [["Home", "/"], [which === "privacy" ? "Privacy Policy" : "Terms of Service"]],
  h1: which === "privacy" ? "Privacy Policy" : "Terms of Service",
}) %>
<%
  const updated = "26 October 2026";
  const mail = site.email ? `<a href="mailto:${site.email}">${site.email}</a>` : `the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>`;
%>
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose" style="margin-inline:auto">
<%# Starting text. Have it reviewed before launch and edit this file. %>
<% if (which === "privacy") { %>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: <%= updated %></p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>This website is run by XPITUDE, a licensed tour operator in Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan. Our office is at <%= site.address.street %>, <%= site.address.city %>, <%= site.address.country %>. In this policy, "we" and "us" mean XPITUDE.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>We only collect what you send us. When you use the enquiry or contact form we receive:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name</li>
        <li>your email address</li>
        <li>your phone or contact number</li>
        <li>your country</li>
        <li>your group size and the kind of trip you are interested in</li>
        <li>any message you write</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you write to us by email or WhatsApp, we also receive what you send there.</p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to your enquiry.</li>
        <li>To plan and run the trip you ask about, and to keep in touch about it.</li>
        <li>To keep a record of our correspondence with you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not add you to a mailing list because you sent an enquiry.</p>

      <h2>Storage and security</h2>
      <p>Enquiries are stored in a password protected database with the companies that host this website and deliver our email, who handle it only on our behalf. Only the XPITUDE team can read it. We keep your details for as long as we need them to answer you and run your trip, and for as long as the law requires.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>The website needs one small cookie to remember your cookie choice. Analytics and marketing cookies are used only if you allow them, and you can change your choice at any time with <button class="legal__cookie" type="button" data-cookie-settings>Cookie Settings</button> (also at the bottom of every page). The typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts, so your browser contacts Google when a page loads.</p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>We never sell your details. When it is needed for your trip, we share only what is necessary with the partners who make it happen, such as hotels, transport, airlines, guides and permit offices. We may also share information when the law requires it.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to <%- mail %> and we will reply.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <%- mail %><% if (site.phone) { %>, or call <%= site.phone %><% } %>.</p>
<% } else { %>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: <%= updated %></p>

      <h2>Using this website</h2>
      <p>This website is published by XPITUDE, a licensed tour operator in Gilgit-Baltistan, with its office at <%= site.address.street %>, <%= site.address.city %>, <%= site.address.country %>. By using it you agree to these terms. The information on it is general guidance for planning a journey and may change without notice.</p>

      <h2>Bookings and enquiries</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Sending an enquiry does not create a booking or an obligation on either side.</li>
        <li>Prices shown as "from" are guide prices per person. The price of your trip is confirmed in a written proposal.</li>
        <li>A booking is made only when you accept a written proposal from us and we confirm it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Payments and deposits</h2>
      <p>A deposit is usually needed to confirm a booking, with the balance due before the trip starts. The amounts, due dates and payment methods for your trip are set out in your proposal and booking confirmation.</p>

      <h2>Cancellations and changes</h2>
      <p>If you need to cancel or change a booking, tell us in writing as soon as possible. The cancellation charges that apply depend on the trip and how close to departure you cancel, and are set out in your booking confirmation. If we have to change or cancel a trip, we will tell you as soon as we can and offer an alternative or a refund of what you paid us for the parts that do not go ahead.</p>

      <h2>Weather, flights and safety</h2>
      <p>Travel in the mountains of Pakistan depends on weather and on things outside our control. Flights to Skardu and Gilgit are often delayed or cancelled in bad weather, roads can close because of landslides or snow, and itineraries may change for safety reasons or government instructions. Our guides may change the route or the plan when they judge it safer. We will always try to find the best alternative, but we are not responsible for extra costs caused by events outside our control.</p>

      <h2>Traveller responsibilities and fitness</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Choose a trip that suits your fitness and experience, and tell us about any medical condition that could affect you on the trip.</li>
        <li>Have a valid passport, visa and travel insurance that covers the activities and altitudes of your trip.</li>
        <li>Follow the instructions of your guide and respect local laws and customs.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>The text, photographs and design of this website belong to XPITUDE or are used with permission, and may not be copied or reused without our written consent.</p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>We take care to keep this website accurate, but we do not guarantee that it is complete or free of errors. As far as the law allows, XPITUDE is not liable for any loss caused by relying on the information on this website. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.</p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Pakistan, and any dispute is subject to the courts of Pakistan.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms can be sent to <%- mail %><% if (site.phone) { %>, or call <%= site.phone %><% } %>.</p>
<% } %>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
<%- include("partials/footer") %>
